ADDRESS: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Introduction_to_Wikipedia
==================================================
[LINK: (Don't be afraid to edit) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Be_bold]  – Anyone can edit  [LINK: (almost) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Protection_policy]  every page; just find something that can be improved and make it better! You can add  [LINK: (content) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Introduction_to_editing_with_VisualEditor/1]  (using  [LINK: (references) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Introduction_to_referencing_with_VisualEditor/1]  to support your claims), upload free-to-use  [LINK: (images) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Introduction_to_images_with_VisualEditor/1] , correct spelling and grammar mistakes, improve prose to make it more readable, or help with  [LINK: (any number of other tasks) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Task_Center] . It's normal for new contributors to feel a little overwhelmed by all of our  [LINK: (policies) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Introduction_to_policies_and_guidelines/1] , but don't worry if you don't understand everything at first. It's fine to use common sense as you edit, and if you accidentally make a mistake, another editor can always fix or improve it later. So go ahead, edit an article, and help make Wikipedia the world's best information source!

[LINK: (Suggest improvements) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Talk_page_guidelines]  – Each article also has a  [LINK: ("Talk" page) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Introduction_to_talk_pages/1] , where you can suggest improvements and corrections to the article.

You're welcome to edit without creating an account, but there are many  [LINK: (benefits of registering an account) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Why_create_an_account%3F] . It's quick and free.

[LINK: (Sign up) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:CreateAccount&returnto=Help%3AIntroduction+to+Wikipedia]

You can test out how editing feels by editing one of the "sandbox" test pages below:

[LINK: (Edit page visually) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Introduction/IP_sandbox]  or  [LINK: (Edit using wiki markup) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Introduction/IP_sandbox] 
 [LINK: (Edit page visually) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:MyPage/Sample_page&veaction=edit&preload=Help:Introduction/main_sandbox&summary=Creating%20sandbox]  or  [LINK: (Edit using wiki markup) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:MyPage/Sample_page&action=edit&preload=Help:Introduction/main_sandbox/preload&summary=Creating%20sandbox&editintro=Help:Introduction/main_sandbox/preload/editintro]

Just type some text and click Publish page when you're happy with the way it looks. Don't worry about breaking anything; these pages are open areas just for experimentation!

Wikipedia has many community pages in addition to its articles.

[LINK: (Task Center) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Task_Center]  – List of tasks with which you can help
 [LINK: (Help pages) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Contents]  – Support and advice
 [LINK: (Community portal) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Community_portal]  – The hub for editors

